{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones","id":1176005,"title":"NonLiving Touchstones.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-14T11:02:03-08:00","id":1176005,"title":"NonLiving Touchstones.","content":"have a few ideas...<br /> <br /> but a lot centers on, is a vampire likely to USE a object touchstone, play with a toy, read a book,carrry a watch whatever, or to keep it in a display case , or such to keep it from being damaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T12:04:25-08:00","id":1176016,"title":"","content":"I feel it should ground the vampire and remind them of the life that once was. The toy is not just a toy, it is a reminder of their childhood and has a story attached. Just like the book, maybe it was a book they were given by someone close or it was a book that inspired a change in their life. The watch may be inherited from your father. These are treasures that ground your character.<br /> <br /> In a similar way my Vampire priest has his church as a touchstone and this specific church has depth of importance to this vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-14T12:18:48-08:00","id":1176021,"title":"","content":"I've also got a Vampire who uses a Church for a touchstone. It's there to remind him of the faith he has in life and tries his best to maintain in death.<br /> <br /> Buildings with a lot of symbolic or personal importance are a good fit, especially as vampires get older and mortal planners start trying to remodel the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T04:06:23-08:00","id":1176919,"title":"","content":"I don't think an object should need to be used for its intended purpose, but should be handled or viewed to get the benefit from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T05:02:07-08:00","id":1176925,"title":"","content":"It depends on the object. Jewelry is a prime example of how it can go either way. Wearing your wedding ring can be a case of forgetting about it until all of a sudden it's damaged or stolen. The same thing as keeping it in a ring box and locked in a drawer, taking it out to clean once a month. Out of sight, out of mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T08:10:59-08:00","id":1176954,"title":"","content":"I have a child vampire that has a locket with her parents' pictures in it for her touchstone. She wears it almost daily, though when she doesnt have it on her, it's locked away somewhere safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T09:13:15-08:00","id":1176974,"title":"","content":"I don't think most player's keep their living touchstones around them at all times, so having a protected place for placing object-based touchstones just makes sense. And, since they won't walk off by themselves or have needs, they are usually easier to protect and hide. That being said, an object can't talk you down from frenzy, and it's harder to have a meaningful interaction with an object to regain Willpower points or to resolve conditions through, so it's a trade off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T06:00:26-08:00","id":1178052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones?p=1176974#post1176974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's harder to have a meaningful interaction with an object to regain Willpower points or to resolve conditions through, so it's a trade off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, do you have any collectables? Mementoes? Do you sometimes take time to pull them out and ... interact with them? Do they help you remember when you picked up that thingie or talked to X at the Y(MCA)?<br /> <br /> The point of an object or place is not because the object or place is what keeps the vamp human, but because the object or place has significance that links them back to their human past, when they did human things with human people. If you've ever seen the Highlander TV series, they did this all the time, with objects reminding the characters of scenes in their past--usually with flashbacks important to the plot.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T06:24:31-08:00","id":1178057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones?p=1176974#post1176974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it's harder to have a meaningful interaction with an object to regain Willpower points or to resolve conditions through, so it's a trade off.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do kindred regain willpower from meaningful interactions with their touchstones? I thought that they had to defend their touchstones from something to actually regain willpower, and that the main benefit of a touchstone was to stave off torpor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 01-22-2018, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T06:32:42-08:00","id":1178060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones?p=1178057#post1178057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do kindred regain willpower from meaningful interactions with their touchstones? I thought that they had to defend their touchstones from something to actually regain willpower, and that the main benefit of a touchstone was to stave off torpor.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Any time the vampire defends her attachment to her Touchstone, she regains a Willpower point. If this defense causes her serious harm, she regains all her spent Willpower points&quot;<br /> <br /> You're mostly right. Defending the Touchstone itself grants full WP, while defending your <i>attachment</i> to your Touchstone grants one WP. Like &quot;convincing&quot; a family it's totally okay for their teen child to hang out with a way too pale creep at night. It still has to be a bit more than just a meaningful interaction (which on the other hand can resolve certain Conditions, and affirm why they're your Touchstone in the first place).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:31:34-08:00","id":1178071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones?p=1178052#post1178052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, do you have any collectables? Mementoes? Do you sometimes take time to pull them out and ... interact with them? Do they help you remember when you picked up that thingie or talked to X at the Y(MCA)?<br /> <br /> The point of an object or place is not because the object or place is what keeps the vamp human, but because the object or place has significance that links them back to their human past, when they did human things with human people. If you've ever seen the Highlander TV series, they did this all the time, with objects reminding the characters of scenes in their past--usually with flashbacks important to the plot.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But in my experience relying on flashbacks as opposed to dynamic characters getting in trouble because of the choices they are making is <i>more difficult</i> to deal with at the table in a couple different ways.<br /> <br /> Objects don't really react like people do, so any danger they get in comes down a lot more to directly GM fiat. And while it's true it all comes down to GM fiat in the end, being able to say to a player (and have them agree) that a touchstone character is acting appropriately, and that those actions have brought 'the trouble' down can be a lot easier to swallow, especially for players used to more antagonistic STs.<br /> <br /> On the other end, should you be running for experienced players and/or writers, allowing flashback narratives to count as important moments / meaningful interactions can become ubiquitous free-passes. Oh, there's an issue? Here's a flashback that addresses this very thing which I didn't even need to pre-consider, I can just inject it whole cloth in retrospect to tick the box.<br /> <br /> Additionally, flashbacks focus the spotlight, usually, on one character/player at a time. Unless you all have backgrounds that your PCs were connected in their preludes, tough to include other characters. That can be mitigated by letting players jump in troupe-style to play one-off characters during that flashback, but again - I think that's a more advanced storytelling technique that makes things a little more difficult to run than standard touchstones.<br /> <br /> Basically, [<i>more difficult</i>] does not equal [<i>impossible</i>], I totally agree. But no, I don't think picking up an heirloom and thinking about it in a scene comes very close to interacting back-and-forth with a person capable of their own decisions and having their own agendas. Your dad's pocket knife is probably not going to fall in love with your Daeva friend and fellow PC. It can't as easily be manipulated (or think it is doing the right thing) and sell some secret to the Mekhet because it thinks it's for your own good, etc.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course, and I do find in my experience that touchstone-places have a lot more dynamic elements to take advantage of than simple touchstone-objects (mostly since places tend to have people in them, while personal objects don't). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T10:38:08-08:00","id":1178101,"title":"","content":"You might have interpreted my post as holding more enthusiasm for objects than it was meant to convey. And flashbacks? Personally I'd <i>never</i> use them during table play and reserve instead solely for solos and written side-bar episodes. Because of all the things you mention. Great for Highlander; hard for the table. <br /> <br /> I've intended to argue that grandfather's knife is more than a knife, not that it's a real substitute for grandfather. That said, however, if you are valuing grandfather's knife enough to make it a touchstone, you can expect that NPCs will know that you care a great deal for that darn knife, and attempt to get &quot;at&quot; it simply for the pleasure of discomfiting you, if nothing else. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T11:58:34-08:00","id":1178137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1176005-nonliving-touchstones?p=1178101#post1178101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've intended to argue that grandfather's knife is more than a knife, not that it's a real substitute for grandfather. That said, however, if you are valuing grandfather's knife enough to make it a touchstone, you can expect that NPCs will know that you care a great deal for that darn knife, and attempt to get &quot;at&quot; it simply for the pleasure of discomfiting you, if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair enough then. And yeah, the way an object embodies being a touchstone can (and should) vary widely. Maybe it's a stand-in for a lost love one, so the object reminds you of them, which in turn helps remind you of your humanity. Maybe it's a doctor's scalpel that connects you to when you truly felt you were serving mankind, before you had to literally prey upon it. Maybe it's a security blanket that you can just cling to and close your eyes and pretend you aren't a monster for a while.<br /> <br /> I've just found it tougher to work in object-touchstones dynamically with the story as opposed to feeling forced to write those side-bars or &quot;I wanna mess with your Touchstone tonight&quot; specific plots. But on the other hand, I've found that object-touchstones are easier to defend. It's nice when something can fit in a pocket, or when you can lock it away in your haven for however long. Those options aren't usually available for people-touchstones (without some humanity checks, at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}